From: Khovanskiy <a@khovanskiy.ru>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 13:00:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 5/7] driver: report the error of a later statement

The loop over the results of a multi-statement query stopped on any
non-zero mysql_next_result, and a positive value - the error of the
next statement - was taken for the end. 'select 1 as a; selec 2'
returned [[{a = 1}]] without an error, and 'insert (100, 1); insert
(100, 2)' succeeded with only the first row written. Now the error is
returned: the earlier statements are done, and the caller must know
that the rest is not.

A failed mysql_use_result of a statement that has a result set is an
error as well, not a statement without rows.
---
 mysql/driver.c | 13 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+)

diff --git a/mysql/driver.c b/mysql/driver.c
index a55b28f..0697759 100755
--- a/mysql/driver.c
+++ b/mysql/driver.c
@@ -418,10 +418,23 @@ lua_mysql_execute(struct lua_State *L)
 			}
 			lua_settable(L, -3);
 		}
+		/*
+		 * No result set: either the statement returns none
+		 * (INSERT) or reading it failed.
+		 */
+		if (res == NULL && mysql_field_count(raw_conn) != 0)
+			return lua_mysql_push_error(L, raw_conn);
 		/* The counts of the last statement are reported. */
 		affected = mysql_affected_rows(raw_conn);
 		insert_id = mysql_insert_id(raw_conn);
 		int next_res = mysql_next_result(raw_conn);
+		/*
+		 * A positive value is the error of the next statement: the
+		 * earlier ones are done, and the caller must know that
+		 * the rest is not.
+		 */
+		if (next_res > 0)
+			return lua_mysql_push_error(L, raw_conn);
 		if (next_res < 0)
 			break;
 	}
